body:
My Express server is running in a docker container with an nginx docker container proxying request to it.

```
Request -> (nginx) -> (express)
```

I've been trying to set up Express so it only trusts the one nginx proxy, but so far I've not been able to get the `trust-proxy` setting to work.
The function I pass to the `trust-proxy` setting seems to never get called in my application.

```ts
app.set('trust proxy', (ip: string) => {
    console.error(`PROXY ADDR: ${ip}`);
    return false;
});
```
With this configuration, the `console.error` never appears in the logs.

Am I doing something wrong here with my configuration, or is `trust proxy` not working as intended?

Minimal reproduction:
```ts
const app = express();

app.set('trust proxy', (ip: string) => {
    console.error(`PROXY ADDR: ${ip}`);
    return false;
});

app.use('*', (_req: express.Request, res: express.Response) => {
    return res.send('Hi');
});

const webServer = createServer(app);
webServer.listen(3731);
```
